        <span class="card-tag tag-blue">Speed</span>
        <h3>Turn wait time into working time.</h3>
        <p>Slow workflows and batch-heavy processes create compounding drag across every team that depends on them. Rebuilding these systems releases time, reduces errors, and puts decisions back in the hands of the people who need to make them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-tag tag-orange">Cost</span>
        <h3>Remove the tax of ageing platforms.</h3>
        <p>Outdated runtimes, unsupported frameworks, and vendor lock-in carry a cost that grows every year — in licences, in specialist knowledge required to maintain them, and in the increasing risk that something will break at the worst possible moment.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card reveal">
        <span class="card-tag tag-purple">Resilience</span>
        <h3>Evolve without accumulating new risk.</h3>
        <p>Modernization done well makes systems easier to change, not harder. Better observability, safer deployments, stronger security posture, and architecture that supports growth — so the next change is less painful than the last.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
